  "title": "Travels of Ibn Battuta",
  "summary": "Ibn Battuta, a Moroccan legal scholar born in Tangier, left home in 1325 aged 21 to make the hajj to Mecca. He passed through Cairo and Mecca in 1326, reached Delhi in late 1334 and served there as a judge under Sultan Muhammad Tughluq, sailed to the Chinese port of Quanzhou in 1345, and was back in Tangier in 1349. His stories were later written down as the Rihla.",
